# KNOWN GAP — `Box[T].get()` for any NON-PRIMITIVE `T` fails to COMPILE on the
# LLVM backend: `llc` hard-errors with a type mismatch.
#
#     Box[P] b = Box(P(7, mkstr(...)))
#     print(b.get().x)
#
#     C     lane: build rc 0, run rc 0, prints 7          <- CORRECT
#     LLVM  lane: build rc 1
#       llc: error: '%v14' defined with type 'i64' but expected 'ptr'
#
# ELEMENT-TYPE AXIS (the discriminator is the payload type, measured 2026-08-27):
#     Box[int]     .get()  -> C ok, LLVM ok
#     Box[String]  .get()  -> C ok (chained), LLVM llc ERROR
#     Box[P]       .get()  -> C ok (chained), LLVM llc ERROR
#
# DISTINCT FROM ITS FAMILY — state the discriminator before merging these:
#   * `t0684` (box_get_bound_to_local_double_free.gg) is a **C-lane RUNTIME
#     double-free** that fires ONLY when the result is BOUND to a local; the
#     CHAINED form `b.get().x` is CORRECT on C.
#   * THIS gap is an **LLVM-lane COMPILE-TIME hard error** that fires on the
#     CHAINED form too — i.e. on the shape that C gets right.
#   * `t0096` is a C-emit symbol collision on `Box__<inner>__drop`; `t0467` is
#     duplicate drop-glue on comprehension trait-box elements. Neither is this.
#
# ⇒ Core #8: `Box[T].get()` on a non-primitive payload is broken on BOTH lanes,
# in two DIFFERENT ways. That is >=2 bugs, not one lane's problem.
#
# ⇒ Core #9 consequence for any Box work: a regression net that reads the box
# back with `.get()` CANNOT be ported to the LLVM lane at all. Nets for Box
# fixes must use a drop-time or `*b` shape instead.
#
# NOTE the sibling operator is CORRECT on both lanes: `print((*b).x)` builds and
# runs clean on C AND LLVM. Bears on the open `*box` retirement question --
# retiring `*box` would migrate every deref site onto the path that does not
# compile here.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): prints 7, on BOTH backends.
# Measured 2026-08-27 at HEAD; orchestrator-verified.

struct P:
    int x
    String s

String mkstr(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Box[P] b = Box(P(7, mkstr("aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa", "bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb")))
    print(b.get().x)
